<title>INDIA: India HDFC falls, FII stake at ceiling.</title>
<headline>India HDFC falls, FII stake at ceiling.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Share prices of India's Housing Development Finance Corporation Ltd (HDFC) fell sharply for the second successive day on Friday after the central bank said holdings by foreign institutional investors (FIIs) have reached the ceiling, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0755 GMT the share was down 269.25 rupees, or 6.33 percent, at 3,985.25 on the Bombay Stock Exchange, after sliding 448.25 rupees on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India said on Thursday FII holdings in the firm had reached 30 percent which is the ceiling set by the government on foreign portfolio purchases in any stock.</p>
<p>--Bombay equities desk +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
